  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien a cappella pop for a four-woman vocal group, voices only. A vocal bass singing round dm and doom syllables on the roots; crisp vocal percussion with a b kick, pf snare and ts hi-hat ticks; two backing voices that stay silent in the verses and enter on the pre-chorus and chorus with close-harmony doo and bah pads in jazz-pop voicings with added ninths. Dry, close and intimate, like four singers around one microphone, consonants crisp and forward, harmonies spread slightly wide. Female lead passed from singer to singer between verses, bright and conversational, with four-part close harmony on the chorus. 104 BPM, E flat major. Bossy, fed up and laughing about it. No instruments of any kind, no drum machine, no autotune, no church-choir reverb, no gospel runs.",
